# Expectation record for 12_preprocessor/006_pragma_and_line.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 006_pragma_and_line
area               = 12_preprocessor
description        = Pragma acceptance observed through properties the standard fixes -- a pushed pragma region must leave the state it found when it is popped, and the C11 _Pragma operator must behave as the directive spelling does -- asserted only as relations so no implementation-defined layout value reaches stdout, together with the effect of a line directive on the source-position macros, including a virtual file name
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
This program contains no undefined and no unspecified behaviour. There is no signed overflow: every
computed value is a small non-negative int, the difference of two line numbers, or the 0-or-1 result
of a comparison. There is no shift operator, no division and no modulo. No object is read before it is
written -- both int locals are initialised at their points of declaration from the line-number macro
-- no object is modified twice between sequence points, no pointer value is converted to an integer,
and no address is printed. No structure object is ever created: the structure types are named only
inside sizeof and alignof, so no member is accessed and no padding byte is read.

ALL INDEXING IS IN BOUNDS, stated at length because it is the one place a bound could be
stressed. Every subscript in the file is applied to a file-name macro's string literal, and there are
three of them across two spellings. Two appear directly in main: index 0, which every non-empty string
has, and index len - 1, where len is the length this same program has just computed for that same
literal. The literal there is the virtual name a line directive supplied above, so len is 14 and both
subscripts name a character of the literal rather than its terminator or anything past it. The third
is s[n] inside the length helper, which is evaluated repeatedly rather than once, and it is included
here rather than treated as an exception: a subscript E[n] is defined as *(E + n), so each evaluation
performs pointer arithmetic on the literal the caller passed and dereferences the result. The helper
starts at n = 0 and advances only after finding that the character it just read was not the
terminator, so the highest index it ever forms is the index OF the terminator -- which is a character
of the array, since a string literal's storage includes its terminating null byte -- and it stops
there. It therefore reads every character up to and including the terminator, forms no pointer past
the end of the literal, and never dereferences one. Its counter is an int and the only strings it
walks are a handful of characters long, so neither an overflow nor a narrowing conversion can arise.
The only other pointer values in the program are the format strings passed to printf and the
file-name macros themselves, all of which point into string literals of static storage duration; no
address-of operator appears, no pointer is stored in an object, and no pointer value is printed. No
aliasing rule is stressed anywhere either: there is no cast between object types and no union.

NO PRAGMA HERE CAN AFFECT WHAT THE PROGRAM PRINTS, and that is what makes the seven assertions about
them sound under every conforming implementation. Each is a RELATION between two identically declared
structures, never a layout value, and each holds under both readings the standard permits. If the
implementation RECOGNISES the packing request, its behaviour is implementation-defined (C11 6.10.6p1)
and the inner structure may be laid out differently, but the pop must restore the state the push saved,
so pack_size_restored and pack_align_restored still read 1. If it IGNORES the request -- which the same
paragraph requires for a pragma it does not recognise -- all three structures are laid out alike and the
same two relations read 1 trivially. pack_size_not_larger and pack_align_not_larger are 1 from the other
side, because packing may shrink a structure or leave it alone and no reading of the request licenses
GROWING one. The three operator relations follow from C11 6.10.9: the _Pragma operator destringizes its
argument and the result is processed as if it were a pragma directive, so whatever an implementation
does with one spelling it must do with the other, which is what pragma_op_matches_directive asserts.
Every relation therefore falls to 0 only for a genuine defect -- a push that is not undone by its pop,
a packing request that enlarges an aggregate, or two spellings of one pragma that disagree.

NO DIAGNOSTIC DIRECTIVE AND NO DIAGNOSTIC-CONTROL PRAGMA APPEARS ON ANY PATH. The file contains exactly
four directives -- two packing pragmas and two line directives -- plus two uses of the operator
spelling, and neither an error directive nor a warning directive is among them, on any branch, because
the file has no conditional compilation at all. An error directive would make translation fail by
design, and a warning directive would write to standard error, which this suite captures into finding
artifacts but never compares; either one would therefore be untestable noise rather than a comparison.
Nothing in the translation unit switches a diagnostic off, either: an earlier form of this program wrote
a diagnostic-control pragma into the source to silence the unknown-pragma diagnostic around the
construct it was testing, which meant the audit gate no longer inspected that construct, and that
suppression has been removed with no replacement anywhere in the file. Measured: every one of the twelve
cells produced zero bytes on standard error.

A line directive numbers the line that FOLLOWS it, so every printing call that reads the line-number
macro sits on the line immediately after its own directive: the printed number is the one the
directive set rather than a function of where the rest of this file happens to sit, and the first two
reads are on adjacent lines, so their difference is one wherever they appear. Measured with the
reference compiler: after the directive selecting 700 the macro reads 700 on the next line and 701 on
the line after it, and after the directive selecting 900 it reads 900 on the next line.

DETERMINISM. Fifteen of the sixteen printed values are an int written with the %d specifier. The
sixteenth is the only %s in the program, and its argument is the file-name macro AFTER a line directive has
supplied a virtual name, so what it prints is a string constant written in this source rather than a
path the harness chose -- which is the whole reason it is safe to print in full. Before that directive
the same macro is reduced to the relation "is not empty" and its value never reaches stdout. Nothing
target-varying, address-derived, time-derived, random or locale-dependent is printed. No plain char
value is printed: char signedness was measured as signed on x86_64 and i686 and unsigned on aarch64
and riscv64, so a plain-char value would diverge for a reason that is not a defect. No raw type width
is printed: sizeof(long) and sizeof(void *) were measured as 4 on i686 and 8 on the other three
targets. No structure size and no alignment is printed as an absolute value. No translation-date and
no translation-time macro is used. Iteration order is fixed by the literal the length helper walks.
main returns 0, inside the 0-125 range the suite requires so that no exit status is truncated.

HERMETICITY. Every input is a literal in this source. Nothing is opened, nothing is read from the
environment, the command line, the clock or the file system, no storage is allocated, and printf is
the only library routine called, so a cell is reproducible from this source and this record alone.

GATE. The default warning gate applies unmodified, no `ub_audit_flags` key appears, and -- the part that
was not previously true -- nothing in the source relaxes the gate from inside either:
-Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror is in force over every line of
this program, including the pragmas under test. Measured clean -- exit status 0 with not one diagnostic
-- with all four reference drivers at -O0, -O1 and -O2 and with the alternate reference compiler, and
clean under -fsanitize=undefined,address -fno-sanitize-recover=all, which compiled, ran, exited 0 and
printed nothing on standard error. Both gates are reference-compiler-only and are never applied to
the compiler under test, so requirement 3's shared-flag discipline is untouched.

NO HEADER IS INCLUDED and printf is declared by hand as `int printf(const char *, ...);`. The compiler
under test bundles only freestanding headers and ships no standard I/O header, so naming one would
fail on its side of the reference comparison while succeeding on the reference side -- a spurious
divergence caused by the test rather than by a compiler.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
THE ONE ASSERTION SHAPE THIS PROGRAM CANNOT MAKE, AND WHY -- RECORDED PER CONSTRAINT C3 RATHER THAN
LEFT AS A SILENT OMISSION.

C11 6.10.6p1 closes with the one thing the standard REQUIRES of a pragma: "Any such pragma that is not
recognized by the implementation is ignored." That is a requirement rather than a permission, so it is
the strongest pragma property a differential oracle could assert -- and it cannot be asserted inside the
mandatory audit gate. The gate is -Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow
-Werror; -Wall enables the unknown-pragma diagnostic and -Werror makes it fatal, so a pragma the
implementation does not recognise -- by construction the only kind the requirement speaks about -- stops
translation before it can be observed at all. MEASURED in this environment with all four reference
drivers and with the alternate reference compiler: an invented namespaced pragma, a pragma carrying no
tokens whatever, and the standard STDC pragma forms (FP_CONTRACT, FENV_ACCESS, CX_LIMITED_RANGE) are each
rejected as an unknown pragma under -Werror.

THE TWO WAYS AROUND THAT WERE BOTH REFUSED, AND THE REASONING IS THE POINT OF THIS PARAGRAPH. A recorded
`ub_audit_flags` deviation cannot express the removal: a deviation may only name members of the default
gate, and the diagnostic in question is implied by -Wall rather than being a member itself, so silencing
it would mean dropping -Wall entire -- dozens of unrelated checks -- and the suite's contract sanctions
only two reductions in any case, the extension area's -pedantic and the narrowing-conversion program's
conversion diagnostics, neither of which is this. Suppressing the diagnostic FROM INSIDE the source with
a diagnostic-control pragma is worse still, and an earlier form of this program did exactly that: it
wrote a push / ignored / pop trio around the invented pragma, which meant the gate no longer inspected
the very construct under test. The gate is what establishes this program's freedom from undefined
behaviour, and a source that neutralises one of its members locally has not satisfied the gate there --
it has stepped outside it. That suppression is removed and nothing replaces it: no directive anywhere in
the file switches a diagnostic off.

WHAT IS EXCLUDED IS THEREFORE ONE ASSERTION SHAPE, NOT THE FEATURE. Pragmas are still exercised on all
twelve cells, in BOTH of their spellings, and what is asserted instead are relations a conforming
implementation cannot fail whichever choice C11 6.10.6p1 leaves it. The subject is the packing region's
push/pop LIFECYCLE, with three identically declared structures -- one before the region, one inside it,
one after the pop -- and the same region written a second time with the C11 6.10.9 _Pragma operator,
whose result "is then processed as if it were a #pragma directive". Seven relations follow, and the
reasoning for each is in this program's own header comment and in ub_notes above; the summary is that a
recognised request must be undone by its pop, an ignored request changes nothing, packing may never
GROW an aggregate, and the two spellings of one pragma must agree. NEITHER SIZE NOR ALIGNMENT IS PRINTED
AS AN ABSOLUTE VALUE anywhere -- only relations between two of them -- so no implementation-defined
layout choice can reach the output.

WHAT THE RELATIONS DO AND DO NOT REPORT, recorded because it decides how a future divergence must be
read, and because it is what stops a maintainer "improving" this program by printing the sizes
themselves. An implementation that recognises the packing request and one that discards it both pass;
the relations fall to 0 only for one that honoured a push without undoing it at the pop, one that
enlarged an aggregate under a packing request, or one whose directive and operator spellings disagree.
An implementation that instead REJECTS one of these pragmas outright does not fail a relation at all:
it fails to translate, and that compile failure is reported as a finding with its reproducer. This is
also why the record carries no expected-divergence marker: both directives in this program are
documented as supported by the compiler under test -- its preprocessor directive handler names pragma
and line among the directives it processes, and its source map tracks line-directive overrides -- so
there is no documented limitation available to cite, and a divergence here must be delivered as a
finding instead of being classified away as expected.

The absolute layout effect of PACKING ITSELF is still not asserted here, and it is not lost from the
corpus: it is exercised by 08_gcc_extensions/005_attribute_packed_aligned.c, whose subject is the packed
and aligned attributes that the repository's own extension inventory does name as supported, which is a
materially stronger authority than a pragma no document mentions.

THE FILE-NAME MACRO IS PATH-DEPENDENT AND IS NEVER PRINTED RAW. The harness copies each program into
its own per-cell workspace, so the real source path differs between cells and between targets, and
printing it would break byte-exact comparison in all twelve of them at once. Before the first line
directive the macro is therefore reduced to the relation "is not empty". Afterwards a line directive
supplies a virtual name written in this source, which is a compile-time constant rather than anything
the file system chose, so it is printed in full, byte for byte, alongside its length and its first and
its last character -- each of those three relations localising a different kind of corruption, a
truncation, a lost first byte or a lost terminator, to its own line. Printing the whole name is the
part that matters: printing only the length and the two endpoints would let any misspelling of the same
length beginning with v and ending with c satisfy every one of those relations, leaving a defect in how
the directive's string literal reaches the macro invisible in every cell. Nothing the file system
chose reaches standard output, so the same bytes are produced from any absolute or relative path the
harness builds in. The recorded length of 14 is the exact character count of the virtual name written
in the directive, and it must be recounted if that name is ever changed. That name designates no
file, is never opened, and must never be created, so hermetic execution is preserved.

WHY THE DIAGNOSTIC-PREFIX EFFECT OF A LINE DIRECTIVE IS NOT ASSERTED. A line directive also changes
the file name and the line number a translator prints in front of its own diagnostics, and that is an
effect a reader might expect a preprocessor test to check. It is deliberately not checked, because
this suite compares stdout bytes and the raw wait status only and never compares standard error:
diagnostic wording legitimately differs between compilers, so comparing it would produce a flood of
divergences that say nothing about code correctness. The directive's effect is therefore observed
solely through the two source-position macros on stdout, which is where it is comparable at all.

WIDTH AND SIGNEDNESS NORMALIZATION, AND THE RESULT IT BUYS. Every printed value is an int or the
virtual name; no raw width, no plain-char value and no layout value is printed. The measured
consequence is what justifies this record's scope: all twelve cells -- four targets times three
optimization levels, each linked statically and executed natively on the host target or under that
target's emulator -- produced byte-identical stdout, exit status 0, and nothing on standard error.
That is why this record restricts no target, disables no oracle and needs no marker: after this
normalization there is no implementation-defined difference left for one of them to describe.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
line_delta=1
pack_size_restored=1
pack_align_restored=1
pack_size_not_larger=1
pack_align_not_larger=1
pragma_op_size_restored=1
pragma_op_align_restored=1
pragma_op_matches_directive=1
real_file_nonempty=1
line_after_directive=700
line_after_next=701
virtual_line=900
virtual_file=virtual_unit.c
virtual_file_len=14
virtual_file_first_is_v=1
virtual_file_last_is_c=1
END
